WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.225
Every project starts with one question: what exactly are we delivering?

00:00:05.345 --> 00:00:10.170
In PlantUML Ultimate, you answer it with a work breakdown structure.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:17.490
Here's a website redesign, split into Discovery, Design and Delivery, with the work packages underneath each phase.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.640
Then the next question arrives: when will it be done, and who is doing it?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.185
Normally, that means retyping everything into a separate planning tool.

00:00:28.305 --> 00:00:35.405
Here, open the Plan tab, choose Create Gantt chart from WBS, give the project a name, pick a start date...

00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:37.275
and that's it.

00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:44.250
You now have one document with two connected diagrams: the breakdown and the schedule.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:50.470
The document navigator lists every link, node to task, so nothing gets lost in translation.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:57.115
And because both are plain PlantUML text, the whole plan can live in Git, right next to your code.

00:00:58.615 --> 00:01:01.065
And here is the Gantt chart.

00:01:01.185 --> 00:01:10.735
Every work package is a task, every phase has its own section, weekends are already closed, and the structure of the breakdown is wired up as dependencies.

00:01:10.855 --> 00:01:15.330
The link icon on each bar tells you it's tied to the WBS.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.730
Now let's plan.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:24.700
Stakeholder interviews are done, so we mark them one hundred percent complete, and assign Alice.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.375
Content inventory is well underway.

00:01:29.495 --> 00:01:32.345
Sixty percent, and Bob owns it.

00:01:33.845 --> 00:01:37.445
Visual design needs more time than the default.

00:01:37.565 --> 00:01:40.590
We make it eight days, and put Carol on it.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.710
Commit the duration, and the bar grows.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:51.035
Now, one click takes us back to the WBS, and this is where the connection pays off.

00:01:51.155 --> 00:01:59.155
Progress from the schedule shows up right inside each box, so you can see at a glance what's done, and what hasn't started yet.

00:02:00.655 --> 00:02:08.155
Hover over any work package to see the plan behind it: the dates, the duration, how far along it is, and who's assigned.

00:02:08.275 --> 00:02:14.200
Your stakeholders get scope and status in one picture, without ever opening the Gantt chart.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.250
And the link works both ways.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:23.945
Rename a work package in the WBS, and the Gantt task follows automatically.

00:02:24.065 --> 00:02:30.965
Structure lives in the breakdown, dates and people live in the schedule, and PlantUML Ultimate keeps them in sync.

00:02:32.465 --> 00:02:34.265
One breakdown.

00:02:34.385 --> 00:02:36.110
One schedule.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.305
Always connected.

00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:42.650
Plan the what, and the when, together, in PlantUML Ultimate.
